WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:05.180
The first trailer for X-Men: Dark Phoenix
has been released, and unsurprisingly, there's

00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:09.680
a lot of anger, sadness, and foreshadowing
packed into the two-minute clip — and we've

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:13.720
watched it a whole bunch of times to help
you uncover all the small details and hints

00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:14.940
you might have missed.

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:16.820
Power flare

00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:22.160
X-Men fans will notice that the trailer boasts
a shot of familiar X-Jet, the Blackbird, hurtling

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:24.500
through space and looking a bit out of control.

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:28.640
In the issues leading up to the original Chris
Claremont-penned comic arc known as The Dark

00:00:28.641 --> 00:00:33.320
Phoenix Saga, the X-Men plummet to Earth in
a damaged ship piloted by Jean Grey.

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:37.400
Jean is unable to shield herself entirely
from solar radiation and the resulting injury

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:42.620
and crash landing lead to the birth of the
Phoenix: sort of Jean, and sort of not-Jean.

00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:43.340
It's complicated.

00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:47.620
In an interview with Entertainment Weekly,
writer and director Simon Kinberg confirmed

00:00:47.620 --> 00:00:52.030
that in Dark Phoenix, the X-Men do go to space,
where they're hit by a solar flare that sparks

00:00:52.030 --> 00:00:53.820
an unexpected change in Jean.

00:00:53.980 --> 00:00:57.500
The trailer seemingly offers a glimpse of
this moment, when we see a shot of what appears

00:00:57.500 --> 00:01:00.380
to be the solar flare right on the tail of
the X-Jet.

00:01:01.640 --> 00:01:02.440
Catching fire

00:01:02.870 --> 00:01:07.700
We saw Sophie Turner's Jean first tap into
her fiery Phoenix powers at the end of X-Men:

00:01:07.720 --> 00:01:08.220
Apocalypse.

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:11.720
In the Dark Phoenix trailer, we're treated
to several shots of Jean aflame.

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:15.800
One shows her completely engulfed in a fire
that appears to get drawn into her body.

00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:19.979
She's sporting an X-uniform, so it's possible
this shot comes from the scene when Jean is

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:21.480
overcome by the solar flare.

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:26.100
We're treated to a few other moments when
fire burns in the irises of Jean's blue eyes

00:01:26.109 --> 00:01:30.749
as she embraces her newfound powers, as in
the final shot of the trailer when flame veins

00:01:30.749 --> 00:01:31.980
creep over her face.

00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:36.219
We also saw Famke Janssen's Jean grappling
with her Phoenix powers throughout The Last

00:01:36.220 --> 00:01:36.780
Stand.

00:01:36.940 --> 00:01:39.240
That Jean failed to control the cosmic force.

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:40.780
Will this Jean have a better outcome?

00:01:41.020 --> 00:01:45.760
The title card at the end of the trailer seems
a bit foreboding, and shows a vaguely Phoenix-shaped

00:01:45.760 --> 00:01:48.220
flicker of light behind a group of clouds.

00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:50.180
Island retreat

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:55.940
In late 2017, it was confirmed that Dark Phoenix
would take Jean to the island of Genosha,

00:01:55.950 --> 00:01:58.759
where Magneto has set up a sort of mutant
refugee home.

00:01:58.759 --> 00:02:02.700
As in the comics, the big-screen version of
Magneto is more complicated than your average

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:07.130
villain, with his struggles against the X-Men
often coming down to opposing ideologies more

00:02:07.130 --> 00:02:09.040
than a truly evil moral code.

00:02:09.340 --> 00:02:13.290
Genosha offers another example of his efforts
to aid mutantkind.

00:02:13.290 --> 00:02:18.310
Genosha is a well-traveled location for mutants
in the source comics, first appearing in 1988

00:02:18.310 --> 00:02:22.310
as a wealthy island nation that achieved its
riches by exploiting the mutants born there

00:02:22.310 --> 00:02:22.960
as slaves.

00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:28.391
Magneto has taken over the island before,
in the 1999 limited series Magneto Rex, during

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:31.180
which he also converted it into a haven for
mutants.

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:33.120
Home free

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:38.000
Kinberg makes his directorial debut with Dark
Phoenix, and based on what we see in this

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:42.750
trailer, Kinberg revisits key moments we saw
in The Last Stand — which he also wrote.

00:02:42.750 --> 00:02:47.290
Rumor has it that studio pressure led to much
of his script for that film being edited down,

00:02:47.290 --> 00:02:48.980
sidelining Jean in the process.

00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:53.080
In Dark Phoenix, Kinberg appears to bring
Jean back to her childhood home as she struggles

00:02:53.080 --> 00:02:57.270
to restrain her emerging Phoenix powers, as
he did in his script for The Last Stand.

00:02:57.740 --> 00:03:00.060
"You have more power than you can imagine,
Jean.

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:03.360
The question is, will you control that power?"

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:11.560
Here, we see Jean confront the X-Men in the
street outside a house in a suburban neighborhood.

00:03:11.560 --> 00:03:15.330
It's likely this marks a turning point in
the film, as the symbolism of Jean destroying

00:03:15.330 --> 00:03:19.480
the home of her late parents can't be denied
in the context of a film that centers on her

00:03:19.480 --> 00:03:23.940
struggle to retain her identity in the face
of her increasingly unrestrained power.

00:03:24.900 --> 00:03:26.160
Sharp dressed team

00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:30.580
During that face-off with her X-Men teammates,
we're treated to our first clear long shot

00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:34.870
of the new X-uniforms — and it should be
a very welcome sight for longtime fans of

00:03:34.870 --> 00:03:35.910
the comics series.

00:03:35.910 --> 00:03:41.170
The design is nearly identical to the revamped
look drawn by renowned artist Frank Quitely

00:03:41.170 --> 00:03:45.170
for Grant Morrison's influential take on the
franchise, which was published as the New

00:03:45.170 --> 00:03:47.660
X-Men series starting in 2001.

00:03:47.750 --> 00:03:51.400
This series also dealt with happenings on
the island of Genosha, but only time will

00:03:51.410 --> 00:03:56.380
tell whether the New X-Men influence on Dark
Phoenix stretches beyond costuming, or if

00:03:56.380 --> 00:04:00.100
this is simply a nod to the characters' illustrious
history on the page.

00:04:00.820 --> 00:04:02.180
Cross X-amination

00:04:02.540 --> 00:04:07.020
Throughout the Dark Phoenix trailer, Professor
X's handling of Jean and her link to her Phoenix

00:04:07.020 --> 00:04:09.080
power is questioned by those closest to him.

00:04:09.160 --> 00:04:10.060
"What did you do?"

00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:12.160
"I had to keep her stable.

00:04:13.060 --> 00:04:14.240
I protected her."

00:04:14.280 --> 00:04:18.640
Mystique isn't the only blue mutant who questions
Professor X's judgement on the matter.

00:04:18.640 --> 00:04:23.420
Later we see Hank McCoy confronting the Professor
and telling him that it's all his fault.

00:04:23.430 --> 00:04:27.499
Whatever Hank is blaming Charles for, it's
clearly pretty serious because a still later

00:04:27.499 --> 00:04:32.520
shot shows the Professor in a standoff opposite
Magneto and several of his mutant team — and

00:04:32.520 --> 00:04:34.980
who's among them but McCoy in his Beast form.

00:04:35.180 --> 00:04:39.160
What could drive this intelligent, measured
academic to take up with Magneto against his

00:04:39.160 --> 00:04:40.240
mentor and friend?

00:04:40.440 --> 00:04:44.920
A close-up of Hank pressing his anguished
blue face to Mystique's may hold the answer.

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:49.630
In The Last Stand, Jean's powers truly moved
beyond her control following her murder of

00:04:49.630 --> 00:04:51.220
Cyclops and the Professor.

00:04:51.449 --> 00:04:55.879
Could her turning point in Dark Phoenix come
when her power leads to the death of Mystique,

00:04:55.880 --> 00:04:58.660
which leads a heartbroken Beast toward the
dark side as well?

00:04:59.600 --> 00:05:00.500
Mystery blonde

00:05:01.220 --> 00:05:06.059
A closely guarded secret of Dark Phoenix is
the identity of Jessica Chastain's character.

00:05:06.060 --> 00:05:09.840
The studio has been tight-lipped, with Kinberg
revealing only that:

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:12.160
"Her character is way way smarter than we
are.

00:05:12.400 --> 00:05:16.999
What she realizes is she can use [Jean Grey]
to manipulate this world, to turn it against

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:17.500
itself."

00:05:17.640 --> 00:05:21.900
Fans have theorized the unknown woman to be
a version of Mastermind, the mutant who invaded

00:05:21.900 --> 00:05:25.260
Jean's mind to brainwash her further toward
the dark side in the comics.

00:05:25.340 --> 00:05:27.840
This was shot down by Kinberg, who did concede:

00:05:27.840 --> 00:05:31.949
"There are elements of the way Mastermind
manipulates Jean that Jessica's character

00:05:31.949 --> 00:05:32.760
does employ.

00:05:33.020 --> 00:05:36.180
[...] You'll see that Jessica's character
has elements of a few different characters

00:05:36.180 --> 00:05:37.060
from the comics."

00:05:37.160 --> 00:05:41.280
Fans wondered if one of those characters could
be Lilandra, the Shi'ar Empress who's been

00:05:41.280 --> 00:05:45.660
entwined in the story of the Dark Phoenix
throughout several of Marvel's comic continuities.

00:05:45.660 --> 00:05:50.240
Fans have also speculated that she could be
based on Emma Frost, AKA the White Queen,

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:53.080
a telepath who went also appeared in the Dark
Phoenix Saga.

00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:57.839
Of course, January Jones already portrayed
Emma Frost in 'X-Men: First Class', so who

00:05:57.840 --> 00:05:59.060
knows if that will be the case.

00:06:00.580 --> 00:06:01.460
Dark duds

00:06:01.940 --> 00:06:06.400
Speaking of Mastermind, one of the most campy
and visually striking moments from The Dark

00:06:06.401 --> 00:06:11.059
Phoenix Saga is Jean Grey "Black Queen" identity,
which she takes on as a result of Mastermind's

00:06:11.060 --> 00:06:12.560
mental manipulations.

00:06:12.710 --> 00:06:16.900
A shot late in the trailer shows Jean wearing
a dark leather jacket with a raised collar,

00:06:16.900 --> 00:06:19.220
along with a more dramatic hairstyle and earrings.

00:06:19.530 --> 00:06:23.740
We see her in a similar getup in her earlier
clip speaking to Chastain in the church.

00:06:23.750 --> 00:06:28.460
Could this be a modified Black Queen ensemble,
a subtle nod to the change in outfit from

00:06:28.460 --> 00:06:29.479
the original comics?

